Backport Ethernet Broadcom 6.6 to Kernel 6.12.
Note:  This is NOT a fix for 'NETDEV WATCHDOG: CPU: 2: transmit queue 0 timed out'.
       It is a temporary workaround to reduce the frequency of the system lockup.  On high load the Broadcom will lock up on kernel 6.12.

1. Download and Extract kernel source 6.6 and 6.12
	mkdir ~/rpi-6.6
	mkdir ~/rpi-6.12

2. From kernel source 6.12 delete the entire broadcom directory:
	rm -fvr ~/rpi-6.12/linux/drivers/net/ethernet/broadcom

3. From kernel source 6.6 copy the entire broadcom directory to kernel source 6.12:
	cp -vR ~/rpi-6.6/linux/drivers/net/ethernet/broadcom ~/rpi-6.12/linux/drivers/net/ethernet

4. Apply patches to kernel source 6.12:
cd ~/rpi-6.12/linux
patch -p1 < bcmgenet.patch
patch -p1 < bcmasp.patch
patch -p1 < bcmasp_ethtool.patch


